From: nuno407 <11352538+nuno407@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/45] ARM: tegra: surface-rt: Describe the UART Bluetooth
 wiring

The 88W8797 on sdmmc3 enumerates only SDIO function 1 (WLAN, 02df:9129).
BT is strapped to UART. The firmware's ACPI tables (Open Surface RT wiki:
https://open-rt.gitbook.io/open-surfacert/surface-rt/uefi/acpi-tables/acpi-ssdt,
SSDT0000.ASL) describe it as BTH0 (NVDAF000): a 115200 baud UART with
RTS/CTS, host-wake on PU6 and an output on PD1. Bluetooth works on UARTC
at 115200 with RTS/CTS.

Drop the bluetooth@2 SDIO node, which never binds. Hog PD1 high
(bt-enable, as UEFI leaves it) and document the wiring on the UARTC node.
BT still needs an SD-UART (BT_UART) build of the 8797 combo firmware. The
linux-firmware image is built with BT_SDIO.
---
 .../nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts   | 29 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
index 2f7a62306..22f3cfcfd 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
@@ -124,6 +124,15 @@ charger-interrupt {
 		};
 	};
 
+	gpio@6000d000 {
+		bt-enable-hog {
+			gpio-hog;
+			gpios = <TEGRA_GPIO(D, 1) GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			output-high;
+			line-name = "bt-enable";
+		};
+	};
+
 	uarta: serial@70006000 {
 		/delete-property/ dmas;
 		/delete-property/ dma-names;
@@ -136,7 +145,13 @@ uartc: serial@70006200 {
 		/delete-property/ reg-shift;
 		status = "okay";
 
-		/* Bluetooth - Marvell 88W8797 */
+		/*
+		 * Bluetooth - Marvell 88W8797, BTH0 (NVDAF000) in the firmware's ACPI tables (Open Surface RT wiki: https://open-rt.gitbook.io/open-surfacert/surface-rt/uefi/acpi-tables/acpi-ssdt): 115200 8N1 with
+		 * RTS/CTS, host-wake on PU6 (edge, active low), enable on PD1. The
+		 * SDIO card exposes only function 1 (WLAN), so BT is strapped to UART.
+		 * BT stays silent with the linux-firmware sd8797_uapsta.bin, which is
+		 * built with BT_SDIO; an SD-UART (BT_UART) combo image is required.
+		 */
 	};
 
 	pwm@7000a000 {
@@ -487,18 +502,6 @@ wifi@1 {
 			interrupt-parent = <&gpio>;
 			interrupts = <TEGRA_GPIO(U, 5) IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 		};
-
-		// TODO test SDIO bluetooth binding
-		bluetooth@2 {
-			compatible = "marvell,sd8897-bt";
-			reg = <2>;
-
-			// interrupt-parent = <&gpio>; TODO
-			// interrupts = <TEGRA_GPIO() IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>; TODO
-
-			marvell,wakeup-pin = /bits/ 16 <0x0d>;
-			marvell,wakeup-gap-ms = /bits/ 16 <0x64>;
-		};
 	};
 
 	sdmmc4: mmc@78000600 {
